      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Hands the conversation to a fresh Claude Code background agent.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "the current conversation should continue in a fresh agent, starting right away"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "summarizes the conversation, then starts a background Claude Code agent with that summary as its prompt"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a new, named agent already working in the same folder, which you manage with claude agents"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike handoff",
              "text": "that skill, by the same author, only writes the summary for you to pass on; this one also launches the next agent"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Claude Code, whose claude --bg command starts background agents"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "only when you invoke it; it sits in its author's in-progress folder, so expect changes"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent writes a summary of the conversation to your system's temp folder, then runs claude --bg with a descriptive name and that summary as the prompt. The new agent starts in the current folder and the command returns at once, so your session carries on while the new one works. The summary names the skills the next agent should load, points to specs, plans, issues, commits and diffs by path or URL instead of copying them, and removes API keys, passwords and personal details, since it becomes the new agent's prompt. Say what the next session is for, and it tailors the summary to that.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2/skills/in-progress/claude-handoff"
