      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Writes an implementation plan from a spec before touching code.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you have a spec or approved design for a multi-step change, before any code is written"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "breaks the work into small test-first tasks, each naming its files, function signatures, tests and the commands that prove it"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a plan file in the repo, checked against the spec, plus a recommendation for how to run it"
            },
            {
              "label": "Written for",
              "text": "whoever implements it, a person or a subagent, assumed never to have seen the codebase or the spec"
            },
            {
              "label": "Next",
              "text": "subagent-driven-development, a fresh subagent per task, or executing-plans, the agent working through it alone"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The plan holds the decisions an implementer couldn't make alone: which files to create or change, the names and types each task shares with others, the exact values from the spec, and the tests that prove each task. Each task is one test cycle: write the failing test, run it and see it fail, write the code, run it and see it pass, commit, with the expected output of every command. The code itself is left to the implementer, except for an algorithm the tests don't pin down. The plan also lists the project-wide constraints and the five likeliest ways real use could break the software that no test covers yet, each then given a test. The agent checks the plan against the spec for gaps, mismatched names and bloat, fixes what it finds, and asks you to review it and choose how it runs: a fresh subagent and review per task, or the agent working through it inline with one review at the end.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/obra/superpowers/tree/bb92a77741419a4ab5f06e711a283343f1ada0c3/skills/writing-plans"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:planning",
          "type:workflow",
          "effect:local",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "planning",
          "agent-workflows"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mattpocock/skills/skills/engineering/improve-codebase-architecture",
      "name": "improve-codebase-architecture",
      "skills.sh": {
        "url": "https://skills.sh/mattpocock/skills/improve-codebase-architecture",
        "installs": 1234823,
        "weeklyInstalls": [43664, 40761, 37241, 42271, 53008, 42480, 38894, 38379],
