      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Implements a piece of work from a spec or tickets.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a spec or ticket is ready and you want the agent to build it now, in this session"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "builds it test-first, type-checks as it goes, runs the full test suite, then reviews the result"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "commits on your current branch, already through a code review"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "two skills by the same author: tdd, its rules for test-first work, and code-review, which checks the diff against the spec and the repo's standards"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "only when you invoke it; the agent won't start it on its own"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short skill that strings two others together. Point it at a spec, a set of tickets or a ticket number; it fetches a ticket from your issue tracker and states its title before starting, and asks if the reference is unclear. It builds with the tdd skill where it can, testing at interfaces agreed with you, runs type checks and single test files as it goes and the full suite once at the end. Then it runs the code-review skill over the work and commits to the current branch. One agent does it all, unlike implement-spec, which hands each ticket of a spec to its own subagent.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2/skills/engineering/implement"
