      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Generates an interactive bash wizard for steps only a human can do, such as credentials or CI setup.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a setup needs steps only you can do, such as copying API keys from dashboards or adding CI secrets"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "writes a bash script that walks you through each step: opens the page, says what to click, saves what you paste"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a script that fills .env and GitHub secrets, with a progress count, confirmations and hidden entry for secrets"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "run the script itself, or take over steps the agent could do on its own"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Here a wizard is an interactive bash script for a manual procedure that's tedious to do by hand and tedious to explain to an AI again: setting up a service, credentials or CI secrets, finding your way around a third-party dashboard, a one-off migration. The agent first reads the repo (.env.example, README, docker-compose, the secrets your GitHub workflows use) and shows you the stages in order, with the value each produces, for you to adjust. It then spells out each stage's path, such as \"Dashboard → Developers → API keys → Reveal → copy\", and asks you or checks the docs rather than invent a step it isn't sure of. A bundled template handles the experience: one stage per screen, how many are left, a confirmation before anything irreversible, opening links on any OS, and saving values to .env and GitHub secrets. The agent checks the syntax and reads the script through to confirm every value lands where it should, but doesn't run it, since that needs you. The script is meant for one run and then deleted, unless you want the setup repeatable and commit it.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2/skills/engineering/wizard"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:engineering",
