      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Blocks destructive git commands with Claude Code hooks.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "Claude Code runs shell commands for you and you don't want it able to push, or to throw away local work"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "installs a hook that stops git push, reset --hard, clean -f, branch -D, checkout . and restore . before they run"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a hook script and a settings entry, for this project or for all your projects"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Claude Code; the hook script uses jq"
            },
            {
              "label": "Keeps working",
              "text": "in every later session, until you remove the hook"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A one-time setup for a Claude Code hook: a script that runs before each shell command and can block it. The agent asks whether to protect this project (.claude/settings.json) or every project (~/.claude/settings.json), copies the bundled script into the matching hooks folder and registers it, merging it into any settings you already have. From then on, a command matching a blocked pattern, including every kind of git push, is stopped before it runs, and Claude gets a message saying it isn't allowed to run it. The agent offers to add or remove patterns, then tests the script with a sample git push command. The script matches text anywhere in the command, so even a commit message that mentions \"git push\" gets blocked.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2/skills/misc/git-guardrails-claude-code"
