        "updated": "2026-10-20",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Sets up Husky pre-commit hooks with lint-staged, type checks and tests.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want every commit in a JavaScript or TypeScript repo formatted, type-checked and tested first"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "installs Husky, lint-staged and Prettier, and writes a pre-commit hook that formats staged files, then runs your type check and tests"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a .husky/pre-commit hook, a lint-staged config, a Prettier config if you had none, and a commit adding them"
            },
            {
              "label": "Works with",
              "text": "npm, pnpm, Yarn or Bun, whichever lockfile it finds"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Husky runs scripts on git events, and lint-staged runs a command on just the files you staged. The agent picks your package manager from the lockfile, installs the three tools as dev dependencies and initializes Husky. The hook it writes formats staged files with Prettier, skipping files Prettier can't read such as images, then runs your typecheck and test scripts over the whole project. If package.json has no typecheck or test script, it leaves that line out and tells you. An existing Prettier config is kept; otherwise it adds one with common defaults. It ends by committing the new files, which runs the new hook once and shows it works.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2/skills/misc/setup-pre-commit"
