        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Tests local web apps with Playwright scripts.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you need to check a web app running on your machine: click through it, take screenshots, read console logs"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "writes Python Playwright scripts against your app, starting your dev servers first and stopping them after"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a script you can rerun, and the screenshots, page content or logs it captures"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python with Playwright, which runs a headless Chromium"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "browser CLIs such as agent-browser or playwright-cli, which the agent drives one command at a time; here it writes and runs whole scripts"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Anthropic's toolkit for testing web apps you're building. The agent writes short Python scripts with Playwright and runs them in headless Chromium. A bundled helper starts one or more servers, say a backend and a frontend, waits until their ports answer, runs the script, then shuts them down. The skill gives the agent a decision path. For a static HTML file it reads the selectors straight from the file. For a live app it first loads the page and waits for network activity to settle, then takes a screenshot or reads the rendered page to find selectors, and only then clicks and types. Examples cover finding buttons, links and inputs, automating local HTML files, and capturing console logs.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/dbd4588f9e1033efb41dad4bef2f7947c8993d44/skills/webapp-testing"
