            }
          ],
          "text": "Caveman is a plugin and skill set that makes agents reply tersely to save tokens. When you run /caveman-stats, a hook installed by the plugin builds a usage report, and the agent prints it as is in a code block, without recomputing or rounding anything. The report shows output and cache-read tokens, response counts and which Caveman mode was active, and it can also total past sessions. It never estimates tokens, percentages or dollars saved, because there's no measured run of the same work without Caveman to compare against. Outside Claude Code it can't read live usage: in Gemini CLI it sends you to /stats model or /stats session, and elsewhere it uses the host's own report or says usage is unavailable.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/juliusbrussee/caveman/tree/bad48a0e1df55e05e3f52249afa35ecc1909ee76/skills/caveman-stats"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:output-style",
          "type:command",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:claude-code",
