            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "a repo linted with ai-hero-cli, the author's course tool, through pnpm"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Built for the author's course repos, where exercises live under exercises/ in numbered folders: a section such as 05-memory-skill-building holds exercises such as 05.02-short-term-memory. Each exercise has at least one of problem/ (the student's workspace, with TODOs), solution/ (the reference code) or explainer/ (concepts only), and each needs a readme.md with real content. You give it a plan, a list of sections and exercises with the parts each needs, and it creates the folders, writes a readme with a title and a description in each, using explainer/ when the plan doesn't say, then runs the course linter, fixes errors until it passes, and commits. It also renumbers or moves exercises. It lays out the structure; writing the exercises is left to you.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/mattpocock/skills/tree/5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2/skills/misc/scaffold-exercises"
