        "skew": 86
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs, critiques, audits, polishes, hardens and animates interfaces.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you build or improve any interface: a landing page, dashboard, form, docs page or native iOS or Android screen"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "acts as a design director with over 20 commands, such as shape, critique, audit, polish, bolder, quieter, harden and animate"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "finished UI code, plus PRODUCT.md and DESIGN.md files that record your product and visual system for later runs"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "a self-contained binary shipped with the skill that loads your project's context; no Node or other runtime needed"
            },
            {
              "label": "Live mode",
              "text": "web only: click an element in your running app and get design variants swapped in live by your dev server"
            },
            {
              "label": "Optional hook",
              "text": "checks each UI file edit for problems such as low contrast, gradient text or drift from your design system"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A large design skill for frontend work. Called with no argument, it suggests the two or three most useful next commands for your project and never runs one without you. init interviews you and writes PRODUCT.md (who the product is for); document records an existing look in DESIGN.md. Every task starts by loading both, then naming the surface's mode: Persuade for landing pages, Operate for app screens, Read for docs, Experience for portfolios. Landing pages get bold, distinctive work; app screens get precision and familiar patterns. Before any edit it loads a quality floor: contrast and spacing checks, every state designed, and stock moves to refuse, such as gradient text, small labels above headings and pages built from identical icon cards. A brief you pin, such as a font, an era or a palette, beats its own taste. Refinement keeps your current look; a redesign replaces it and rewrites DESIGN.md. Unlike Hallmark, which rotates through a catalog of page shapes and themes, it works from your product brief and the page's purpose. The repo also publishes polish, critique, audit and animate as standalone skills; this one includes them as commands.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable/tree/dad8dbb3aac21ad1fa236c110315ef4abece23e8/plugin/skills/impeccable"
        },
