      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Extracts design tokens from a public website into starter files.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're starting a project and want its design tokens seeded from a public website you like"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "runs the extract-design-system tool on the URL and summarizes the colours, fonts and spacing, radius and shadow scales it found"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "design-system/tokens.json and tokens.css, plus the raw and cleaned-up extraction data in .extract-design-system/"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node, for npx, and a Chromium browser download through Playwright, which it runs as its first step"
            },
            {
              "label": "Won't",
              "text": "build components, promise a pixel-perfect copy, or touch your existing styles without asking"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A small wrapper around the extract-design-system command-line tool. You give it a public URL and say whether you want just the extraction or starter token files too. The agent installs Playwright's Chromium, runs the tool, then tells you the likely primary, secondary and accent colours, the fonts, and any spacing, radius and shadow scales. If you already have an extraction, it can regenerate the token files from it without fetching the site again. It's meant as a starting point, not a source of truth: it warns that one page doesn't prove a whole design system and that dynamic sites may extract only partly, it won't invent components or semantic tokens it didn't find, and it asks before changing any app code, styles or config. Unlike the Hallmark design skill's study command, which describes a site's page structure and type pairing in a report, it gives you token files.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/arvindrk/extract-design-system/tree/1873741ba8dea755e35e6e15134f7918cd58e036/skills/extract-design-system"
        },
        "tags": [
