      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Applies one of ten preset themes to slides, docs and landing pages.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a slide deck, document, report or landing page needs one consistent look"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "shows you a PDF sampling ten preset themes, waits for your pick, then applies its colors and fonts throughout"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "your deck or page restyled with one color palette and one pair of header and body fonts"
            },
            {
              "label": "Themes",
              "text": "ten, from Ocean Depths and Forest Canopy to Midnight Galaxy, each with hex colors, fonts and the content it suits"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also",
              "text": "invents a new theme from your description when none fits, and shows it to you before applying it"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A style library rather than a design process. Each of its ten themes is a small file with a color palette in hex codes, a header and a body font, and the kinds of content it suits. Ocean Depths, for instance, pairs deep navy and teal with DejaVu Sans for corporate and financial decks; Midnight Galaxy uses deep purples for entertainment and gaming. The agent shows you theme-showcase.pdf, a visual sample of all ten, asks which one you want and waits for a clear answer. It then reads that theme's file and applies the colors and fonts consistently across every slide or page, checking contrast and readability. If none fits, it makes up a new theme from your description, names it in the same spirit and shows it for approval first. It only styles: the deck, document or page itself is made by the agent or another skill.",
