        "updated": "2026-10-20",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Applies design-engineering details that make interfaces feel polished.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're building or reviewing UI that works but feels slightly off"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "applies 19 small rules, such as matching corner curves on nested boxes, centering icons by eye, shadows over borders, and subtle press animations"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "polished UI code, or a review: findings with severity, file, before and after, then a verdict"
            },
            {
              "label": "Review modes",
              "text": "quick, at most 5 high or medium findings on the main user path; full, up to 15 across typography, surfaces, animation, icons and performance"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike frontend-design",
              "text": "which sets a visual direction, it fixes details within the styling you already use"
            },
            {
              "label": "Runs",
              "text": "when the agent builds or reviews UI, or when you ask"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A checklist of the small details that, added up, make an interface feel finished. Some are exact: the outer corner radius equals the inner radius plus the padding; buttons shrink to 0.96 when pressed, never below 0.95; numbers that change use fixed-width digits so the layout doesn't jump; icons swap with a set scale, fade and blur; images get a faint 1px outline in pure black or white. Others are judgement: shadows for depth, borders for structure; exits softer than entrances; no custom animation on actions people repeat constantly; clickable areas of at least 44 by 44 pixels on touch screens. Every fix is written in the project's existing styling, whether Tailwind, CSS or CSS-in-JS. In a review it checks every state, such as hover, focus and loading, watches animations slowed to 10% in the browser's dev tools, cites the file and line of each finding, lists candidates it considered and rejected, and ends with Block, Needs changes or Approve.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/jakubkrehel/make-interfaces-feel-better/tree/35545ea1512ad59fa463e6b1f95ca9c052981fe6/skills/make-interfaces-feel-better"
        },
        "tags": [
          "category:design",
          "type:guidelines",
          "effect:none",
          "needs:none",
          "by:community",
          "design",
          "animation"
        ]
      }
    },
