        "updated": "2026-10-23",
        "skew": 11499
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Designs pages that look made, not generated.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want an agent-built landing page, app screen or component that doesn't look AI-generated"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "asks about audience, purpose and tone, then picks a named page layout and theme that differ from its previous builds"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "the page code, a tokens.css file of its colours, fonts and spacing, and a .hallmark/log.json of past choices"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also does",
              "text": "audit (ranks a page's telltale AI-design habits, no edits), redesign (new structure, same content) and study (reads a design's structure and type from a screenshot or URL)"
            },
            {
              "label": "Self-check",
              "text": "a 58-point checklist before handing back: no invented stats or testimonials, no italic headings, no fake browser frames, clean layout down to 320px wide"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Hallmark is a strict design rulebook for agents building web pages. Its signature is structural variety: two pages for two briefs shouldn't share the same hero, three feature cards, call to action and footer. For a new page, the agent first reads your project's fonts, colours, spacing and framework and keeps them unless you say otherwise, then always asks about audience, purpose and tone (say \"go ahead\" and it guesses and tells you what it picked). It chooses a page shape from a catalog of 21, such as Bento Grid or Long Document, plus a nav, a footer and a theme, avoiding what it used last in this project, and shows a short preview before writing code. Every colour and font must come from a named token, every button gets eight states such as hover, loading and error, and motion respects reduced-motion settings. A single component gets its file plus a preview page showing all eight states. In an existing codebase it edits in place and asks before deleting anything. On request it locks the result into a design.md that later pages follow. study never copies pixels and won't study template-marketplace pages such as ThemeForest's.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/nutlope/hallmark/tree/13ac0ec7e148655948100b6396439e481361d690/skills/hallmark"
        },
        "tags": [
