              "label": "You get",
              "text": "one Markdown file per issue, with its title, labels, assignees, milestone and state at the top"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the gh-issue-sync CLI, which this skill ships with, run inside a git repository"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A short command reference for the gh-issue-sync CLI. After init in a git repository, pull fetches open issues, and closed ones with --all, into .issues/open/ and .issues/closed/: one Markdown file per issue, named after its number and title, such as 42-fix-login-bug.md. A header block holds the title, labels, assignees, milestone, state and links to related issues; the body is the issue text. You or the agent edit these files, status and diff show what changed, and push sends it, with --dry-run to preview first. A new issue gets a placeholder number until push creates it on GitHub, then the file is renamed and mentions of it in other issues are updated. To comment, you write a .comment.md file next to the issue; it's posted on push, then deleted. Pull skips files that conflict with local changes unless you force it.",
