            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike webapp-testing",
              "text": "Anthropic's Playwright skill, where the agent writes whole Python scripts, this runs one command per action and shows the result each time"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also does",
              "text": "mocks network requests, saves logins and cookies, connects to a Chrome you already have open, and lets you mark up a live page for design feedback"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Microsoft's skill for its Playwright command-line tool. The agent opens a browser and sends commands such as goto, click e15, fill or press. After each one it gets a fresh snapshot of the page, saved to a file, listing its elements with IDs it can target next; CSS selectors and Playwright locators work too. Beyond clicking, it handles tabs, cookies and storage, saved login state, emulating dark mode or reduced motion, mocked network routes, console and network logs, tracing, and video with each action labelled on screen. Because every action prints its Playwright code, the agent can plan, generate and repair tests: it starts a failing test paused in the debugger, connects to it and explores until the fix is clear. In annotate mode you draw boxes on the live page and type comments, and the agent receives them with a screenshot. Named sessions keep several browsers apart.",
