              "text": "a task needs a real browser: pages built by JavaScript or behind a login, forms, screenshots, network capture"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "drives a full browser through the CLI of BrowserAct, a browser-automation service, with separate browsers for parallel accounts"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "page content, screenshots and captured network responses, or the task done in the browser"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the browser-act CLI, installed with uv on Python 3.12 or later"
            },
            {
              "label": "Asks first",
              "text": "before installing, creating a browser, logging in, submitting forms or uploading files"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The agent navigates, clicks and types, fills forms, uploads files, takes screenshots, captures the page's network requests and opens several pages in parallel. A quick fetch returns a page's content after its JavaScript has run, without opening a browser session, and the skill tells the agent to prefer it over built-in web tools. Each browser is isolated, so several accounts can run side by side, and you can take over a step by hand in a visible window, or from any device through a link. When a page shows a verification challenge, such as a captcha, the agent can send the challenge image to BrowserAct's solving service, with your permission; cookies and page content stay on your machine. Its full instructions come from the installed CLI, so they always match your version. Its sibling browser-act-skill-forge turns a site you explore into a reusable skill.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/browser-act/skills/tree/11c057b03f92101642cadc9f840564574120d184/browser-act"
        },
