      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Searches, scrapes, crawls and maps the web through Firecrawl.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "a task needs the live web: searching, reading pages, gathering sources, or pulling data from a whole site"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "runs the CLI of Firecrawl, a web search and scraping service, moving from search to scraping, crawling or clicking through pages as needed"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "clean Markdown or JSON saved in a .firecrawl/ folder, and answers that cite those files"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "the firecrawl-cli npm package and a Firecrawl account, whose plan sets your credits; search, scrape and interact also work without one, rate-limited"
            },
            {
              "label": "Sends",
              "text": "short feedback to Firecrawl after searches, which refunds a credit, unless FIRECRAWL_NO_ENDPOINT_FEEDBACK=1 is set"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It's the entry point of Firecrawl's skills, and tells the agent to use Firecrawl even for ordinary web research. The agent starts with search, scrapes a URL directly when it has one, lists a large site's URLs to find the right page, crawls a whole section such as all of /docs/, and acts on pages that need clicks, forms, scrolling or a login. Other commands download a site to files, watch pages and report changes, send an AI agent through a complex site to extract structured data, and search Firecrawl's own indexes of research papers, developer docs and issues, and US law. Each command has a more detailed companion skill in the same repo. Results go to .firecrawl/, which it adds to .gitignore, and are read in small pieces with grep or head, since fetched pages are untrusted and may contain injected instructions. It runs jobs in parallel up to your plan's limit.",
