      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Creates animated GIFs optimized for Slack.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want an animated GIF or custom emoji for Slack, like \"a cat doing a spin\""
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "draws each frame in Python with Pillow, eases the motion so it speeds up and slows down naturally, then assembles and checks the GIF"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a GIF file sized for Slack, 128×128 for an emoji or 480×480 for a message, which you upload yourself"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Python with pillow, imageio and numpy"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't include",
              "text": "ready-made graphics or emoji fonts; everything is drawn from shapes, or from an image you upload"
            }
          ],
          "text": "A toolkit plus know-how for Slack GIFs. The agent draws every frame from simple shapes with Pillow, or starts from an image you upload, either animating it or borrowing its colors and style. Bundled helpers do the rest: a GIF builder collects frames and saves them with few colors to keep the file small, a validator checks the file against Slack's limits, easing functions such as ease-out, bounce and elastic smooth the motion, and small functions draw gradients, stars, circles and text. The skill describes how to make common animations, which can be combined: shake, pulse or heartbeat, bounce, spin, fade, slide, zoom and particle bursts. It pushes for polish too: thicker lines, layered shapes, highlights and glows, vivid contrasting colors. Slack's targets are 10 to 30 frames per second, 48 to 128 colors, and under three seconds for an emoji; it shrinks a file further only if you ask.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/dbd4588f9e1033efb41dad4bef2f7947c8993d44/skills/slack-gif-creator"
