      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Creates and edits Word documents, including tracked changes and comments.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you need a Word document written, read or edited, including tracked changes and comments"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "writes new documents with the docx JavaScript library, and edits existing ones by changing their XML directly"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a .docx file, which the agent renders to page images and looks at before handing over"
            },
            {
              "label": "Handles",
              "text": "tracked changes under an author name you choose, comments and replies anchored to text, and a clean copy with changes accepted"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node, pandoc, LibreOffice and Poppler; it installs the docx library only if it's missing"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Anthropic's skill for Word files, which treats a .docx as what it is: a ZIP of XML files. New documents are written as a script using the docx npm library, and the skill lists the traps the agent would otherwise fall into, such as A4 instead of US Letter by default, tables that need widths set twice, typed bullet characters and line breaks inside a paragraph. That library can't open existing files, so for edits the agent unzips the document, merges the fragments Word splits text into so phrases can be found, edits the XML in place, zips it back and checks it against the format's rules. When editing with tracked changes, every change is wrapped as a tracked insertion or deletion, and the same check flags any edit made without tracking. A helper script adds comments. Reading is done by converting to Markdown with pandoc, and old .doc files are converted first. Its siblings pdf, pptx and xlsx cover the other office formats.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/dbd4588f9e1033efb41dad4bef2f7947c8993d44/skills/docx"
        },
