        "updated": "2026-10-20",
        "skew": 0
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Diagnoses technical SEO issues on a site.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "your site isn't ranking, traffic dropped, or you want an SEO health check"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "checks whether Google can crawl and index the site first, then speed, mobile, HTTPS, page tags, content and links"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "an audit report: top issues, each finding with its impact, evidence and fix, and a prioritized action plan"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also covers",
              "text": "sites in several languages, local businesses and title-tag rewrites"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "the same repo's skills for planning content or building pages at scale, it diagnoses the site you already have"
            }
          ],
          "text": "An SEO audit done in order of what blocks ranking most: can Google find and index the pages, is the site fast and working on mobile, are titles, descriptions, headings and internal links right, does the content deserve to rank, and does the site have authority. It first asks about the site, its goals, recent migrations and whether you have Google Search Console access, and reads your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes). Before reporting structured data as missing, it checks in a real browser, since a plain page fetch misses markup that JavaScript adds. Once the basics are sound, it points to pages already sitting just below the top of the results, in positions 8 to 20, as the quickest wins. It lists common problems by site type: SaaS, e-commerce, blogs, multilingual and local businesses. It only reports: fixing structured data or optimizing for AI search is left to other skills in the repo.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/e85f3cbc2e4a79bf33b2a12e9bdd9087d414735b/skills/seo-audit"
        },
