          "text": "Works best with a photo of your product. Its ten modes are a plain studio shot, the product in a real scene, a close-up with hands or a face, a vertical Pinterest pin, a wide website banner, a social carousel, a pack of ad variants, an AI model wearing the product, a surreal floating or splash shot, and a restyle of an existing image for a new mood or season. Before generating, it asks a few questions with set options, such as how many images, what style and where they'll be used, skipping any you've already answered. It then sends a short brief, and Higgsfield turns it into the final prompt from its own photography templates; the skill warns that writing the prompt by hand gives noticeably worse images. Several variants differ in lighting, angle and palette rather than being near-copies. The reply is just the image links.",
