        "skew": 4
      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Plans what content to create and why.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you don't know what to write about, or need a content plan for your blog or site"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "mines customer, keyword and competitor research for ideas, scores each one, and decides what to make first"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "3-5 core topics to own, each with a cluster of linked articles, and a ranked list of pieces with target keyword and buyer stage"
            },
            {
              "label": "Skips",
              "text": "search articles that would add nothing the current top results don't already have"
            },
            {
              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "copywriting from the same repo, it decides what to write, not the words"
            }
          ],
          "text": "It plans content that is searchable (answers what people already look up), shareable (creates demand and gets passed around), or both, with search as the foundation. After reading your product marketing context if you have it (a shared file on your product, audience and positioning that the repo's product-marketing skill writes) and asking about your business, customers and resources, it mines ideas from keyword exports, sales-call transcripts, surveys, Reddit and Quora, competitors' blogs and support tickets. Topics are mapped to buyer stages, from \"what is\" through \"vs\" and \"pricing\" to \"how to use\". Each idea is scored on customer impact (40%), fit with your product (30%), search potential (20%) and effort (10%). It suggests a calendar of 60% searchable, 30% shareable and 10% experimental pieces, and plans distribution: one strong piece reused across channels, moving readers from other people's audiences and social platforms toward your own email list and blog.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/e85f3cbc2e4a79bf33b2a12e9bdd9087d414735b/skills/content-strategy"
