              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "seo-audit from the same repo, it plans new pages instead of diagnosing existing ones"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Programmatic SEO means generating many pages from one template and a dataset, each aimed at a variation of the same search, like \"crm for real estate\" or \"slack asana integration\". The skill picks from 12 such page types: templates, best-of lists, unit conversions, comparisons, examples, locations, personas, integrations, glossaries, translations, directories and profiles, which can be combined (\"best coworking spaces in San Diego\"). It then works through the keyword pattern and its search volume, where the data comes from (your own data beats public data anyone can copy), the template, a category page linking to each generated page, which thin pages to keep out of Google, and whether your CMS can hold and render the pages on your main domain. Its rule is that 100 great pages beat 10,000 thin ones. A pre-launch checklist covers unique value, titles, structured data, sitemaps and crawlability, followed by what to watch after launch.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/coreyhaines31/marketingskills/tree/e85f3cbc2e4a79bf33b2a12e9bdd9087d414735b/skills/programmatic-seo"
