              "label": "Unlike",
              "text": "the seo-audit skill, which applies an SEO checklist by hand and ends with recommendations, it runs a crawler and edits your code"
            }
          ],
          "text": "squirrelscan is a website auditing CLI, and this skill turns its report into a fix loop. The agent audits the live site when there is one, since only that shows true rendering, speed and redirects, starting with a quick 25-page pass, then a 100-page pass that samples each page template, or a 500-page full crawl before sign-off. It reads squirrel's compact text report made for agents, shows you the score, grade and worst issues, and lists the fixes it can make. Once you approve, it traces each finding to the template, component or content file behind it, fixes in batches, checks the project still builds, and re-audits until it reaches a target set by the starting score: under 50 aims for 75, 50 to 70 for 85, 70 to 85 for 90, above 85 for 95. Errors come first, then high-ranked warnings. It can diff against an earlier audit to prove progress or catch regressions. Installation, login, pricing and shareable reports are covered by a separate squirrelscan skill.",
