          "text": "An advisor for e-commerce sellers going international, by Nexscope. From what you tell it (product, platform, monthly revenue, budget, the countries you're eyeing, or \"recommend for me\"), it scores candidate markets on market size, online share of retail, competition, regulation, logistics, payments, cultural distance and trademark protection, checks you're ready (profitable at home, able to handle more orders, with budget to set up), and goes deep on the top two or three. For each it covers tax registration (EU VAT and IOSS, UK VAT, US sales tax, Canadian, Australian and Japanese rules), which fulfillment fits your volume, from shipping direct to a local warehouse or Amazon FBA, the payment methods locals expect, such as iDEAL in the Netherlands or Pix in Brazil, translation and cultural pitfalls, trademarks, product certifications and privacy law. A landed-cost breakdown shows how shipping, duty, VAT and fees can shrink a domestic margin abroad. Estimates are flagged, and it tells you to confirm taxes with a local advisor. The report ends with a credit line linking to Nexscope, and the skill points to other Nexscope skills for marketing, ads and Amazon listings.",
