      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Creates validated architecture, sequence and data-flow diagrams as interactive HTML.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you want a diagram of a system, flow, database or history, from a description, Mermaid code or a real codebase"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "picks the diagram type, draws it, then checks it automatically, including in a real browser, and fixes what fails"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a standalone HTML file, with dark and light themes, motion, and export to image, SVG or WebM"
            },
            {
              "label": "Diagram types",
              "text": "architecture, workflow, sequence, data flow, status changes, database tables, classes, tree, timeline, and where a request's time went"
            },
            {
              "label": "Also makes",
              "text": "one-page explainers that answer a question, conclusion first, when you ask for a page"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needs",
              "text": "Node.js"
            }
          ],
          "text": "You describe a system, paste Mermaid code, or point it at a repo, and it picks one of ten diagram types. For a codebase it traces the behavior you asked about through the source and keeps that evidence with the diagram. Before handing over, it runs automated checks, including one in a real browser, and repairs and reruns when one fails. Mermaid is read for its meaning and redrawn in Archify's own style. Each diagram gets its own folder under .archify/ in your working directory, and the reply is a link to the HTML plus a line on how to read it. The second mode is the explainer: ask for an answer as a page, and it builds one that leads with the conclusion, then sections with tables, steps, diagrams and charts. Afterwards it offers, once, to make such pages unasked in future; if you agree, it adds a line to your agent's global instructions file, such as ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. It doesn't build dashboards.",
