      },
      "agentReview": {
        "description": "Maps a deep-learning repo and plans a README-first reproduction.",
        "tldr": {
          "glance": [
            {
              "label": "Use it when",
              "text": "you're starting to reproduce a deep-learning repo and want it mapped before anything runs"
            },
            {
              "label": "It does",
              "text": "reads the README and setup files, lists the documented commands and sorts them into inference, evaluation, training or other"
            },
            {
              "label": "You get",
              "text": "a short repo summary, a command list, the smallest documented run worth trying first, and the ambiguities and risks"
            },
            {
              "label": "Doesn't",
              "text": "install anything, download data or model weights, run the commands or patch code"
            },
            {
              "label": "Usually called by",
              "text": "RigorPilot's main skill, which reproduces a research repo from its README, as its first step"
            }
          ],
          "text": "The first step in RigorPilot, a set of skills that reproduces deep-learning research code by following its README. It reads the README and the usual project files (requirements.txt, environment.yml, pyproject.toml, setup.py, Dockerfile) and looks for clues in folders such as configs, scripts and examples. Commands are sorted by what they do: running the model on inputs (inference), scoring it on a benchmark (evaluation), training or fine-tuning it, or other steps like installing, downloading and preprocessing. It's conservative: explicit README commands win over guesses from file names, guessed categories are marked as inferred, and ambiguity is written down rather than settled by assumption. The run it recommends is the smallest one the README documents that can still be trusted, and you can steer it with a priority, such as inference first. Setup and the run itself are left to other RigorPilot skills.",
          "permalink": "https://github.com/lllllllama/rigorpilot-skills/tree/fb3ccdf5aa64b1fa5b1d0463e666a8bc8bc26e01/skills/repo-intake-and-plan"
