          "text": "Anthropic's guide to building MCP servers. First the agent reads the MCP spec and the official SDK docs, then the service's API, and lists the endpoints to cover, most common first. Then it builds shared pieces (an authenticated API client, error helpers, pagination) and each tool: typed, validated inputs, structured output, consistent names with a common prefix, error messages that tell the agent what to try next, and hints marking a tool as read-only or destructive. It builds the server and tries it in MCP's inspector tool. Last comes the evaluation: 10 realistic questions about real data, each needing many read-only tool calls and having one stable answer. A bundled script runs them through Claude against your server, to show whether an agent can actually get work done with it. Separate guides hold the detailed patterns for TypeScript and Python.",
